  Those builds are statically linked, as upstream compiles them (with its
  pcre2 feature, and jemalloc as the allocator on musl), so they also carry
  PCRE2 10.46 (BSD-3-Clause with the PCRE2 exception), jemalloc 5.3.1
  (BSD-2-Clause), the musl C library (MIT), LLVM's libunwind and compiler-rt
  (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions), the Rust standard library with its
  compiler-builtins (MIT and Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions) and ripgrep's
  crate dependencies, each under the permissive license it states.
